        "text": "I'll design a SQL query to find duplicate email addresses in a typical users table.\n\n## Basic Query to Find Duplicate Emails\n\n```sql\nSELECT email, COUNT(*) as email_count\nFROM users\nGROUP BY email\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 1\nORDER BY email_count DESC;\n```\n\n## More Detailed Query with User Information\n\nIf you want to see which users have duplicate emails:\n\n```sql\nSELECT u1.email, u1.id, u1.username, u1.created_at\nFROM users u1\nINNER JOIN users u2 ON u1.email = u2.email AND u1.id != u2.id\nORDER BY u1.email, u1.id;\n```\n\n## Query Using Window Function (for better performance on large datasets)\n\n```sql\nWITH email_counts AS (\n    SELECT \n        email,\n        COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY email) as email_count\n    FROM users\n)\nSELECT DISTINCT email, email_count\nFROM email_counts\nWHERE email_count > 1\nORDER BY email_count DESC;\n```\n\n## Query to Find Duplicates with Case-Insensitive Matching\n\n```sql\nSELECT LOWER(email) as normalized_email, COUNT(*) as email_count\nFROM users\nGROUP BY LOWER(email)\nHAVING"
